[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605302358-social-security-real-world-delivery-pipeline", :adr/title "ADR-2605302358: §1.16 Social Security — Real-World Delivery & Outreach Pipeline (kotoba persist → compute → openmail → atproto publish → social post → MCP expose)", :adr/status "proposed", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2605302358: §1.16 Social Security — Real-World Delivery & Outreach Pipeline\n\n**Status**: proposed\n**Date**: 2026-05-30\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (author), Council Lv6+ ≥3 (ratify pipeline) + Council Lv7+ (live activation, gated on §1.16 identity-level ratify per ADR-2605302357 §3) + 30-day public objection\n**ADR Hierarchy**: Child of ADR-2605302357 (§1.16 doctrine). Integration ADR — wires existing substrate (kotoba / openmail / feed-post / MCP facade / membership ritual / toritate / Public Fund) into one human-facing flow. Introduces new cells + lexicons; **no new Tier-B did:web actor, no new Solidity**.\n\n# Context\n\nADR-2605302357 fixed Charter §1.16 (人類の社会保障): humanity's social security, covenantal-universal, entered by a conversion (悔い改め・バプテスマ・得度 = social death and rebirth), with 信者 Level 0 admitted by a **permanent commitment vow recorded to kotoba + IPFS + token** (§1.16.3a). That ADR is a *doctrine* — it does not specify the concrete machinery by which a **real human** (a) discovers the open door, (b) performs the vow, (c) has it persisted and computed, (d) is **notified by email**, (e) **appears publicly** on atproto, and (f) is **reachable by agents** over MCP.\n\nThe author directive (2026-05-30): *\"実際に実世界に human に影響するように設計をまとめて — kotoba で永続化, compute, mailer などでメール送信, atproto で公開, social post, mcp 公開\"* — asks for exactly that: the real-world delivery pipeline, built only from charter-compliant substrate, that already exists in this monorepo:\n\n| Need | Existing substrate | ADR |\n|---|---|---|\n| 永続化 (persist) | kotoba EAVT datoms + IPFS pin | 2605262130 / 2605171800 |\n| compute | kotodama Pregel cells + kotoba WASM actors (live on :8077) | 2605302355 / 2605301625 |\n| mailer (メール送信) | **openmail** — atproto MST-native mail + SMTP bridge + on-chain postage | 2605172200 |\n| atproto 公開 + social post | **feed-post membrane** + feed-discover projection (`app.bsky.feed.post`) | 2605231902 |\n| MCP 公開 | **kotodama MCP tool facade** | 0087 |\n| token (SBT) + benefit | Adherent SBT + Public Fund + tithe | 2605172600 / 2605192145 / 2605192130 |\n| inference | Murakumo loopback LiteLLM only | 2605215000 |\n| no platform key | member/operator-signed | 2605231525 |\n| PII confidentiality | `com.etzhayyim.encrypted.*` envelope | 2605181100 |\n\nThis ADR is the **integration design** that connects them. **Critical**: live outward-facing actions (sending real email to humans, publishing public social posts, minting SBTs, delivering benefits) are **hard to reverse and touch real people**. R0 here is **design + scaffold only**; every live action is gated (§7).\n\n# Decision\n\n## 1. The pipeline — six stages, real-world human effect\n\nA human moves left→right. Each stage names its substrate and its concrete real-world effect. The pipeline coordinator is a cell-group (working handle **産土 ubusuna**, \"birth-guardian\" — fits social-death-and-rebirth + ongoing protection); it is a set of kotodama cells, **not** a new did:web actor.\n\n```\n[0 OUTREACH] → [1 VOW] → [2 COMPUTE] → [3 NOTIFY] → [4 PUBLISH] → [5 SOCIAL] → [6 MCP]\n  feed-post     member-     kotodama/     openmail     atproto       feed-post    MCP facade\n  + MCP         signed      kotoba WASM    mailer       MST + agg     (ongoing)    (read +\n  discovery     vow         compute        (email)      metric                     signed-write)\n                kotoba+IPFS\n                +SBT\n```\n\n### Stage 0 — Outreach / 招き (the door is open)\n- **Substrate**: feed-post membrane (ADR-2605231902) posts the §1.16.9 public declaration as `app.bsky.feed.post`; etzhayyim.com landing (DID-resolved); MCP discovery tool (Stage 6).\n- **Real effect**: a human anywhere sees the open invitation.\n- **Constraint**: broadcast + pull only. **No microtargeted advertising, no Meta Pixel / GA4-ads / affiliate, no profiling** (ADR-2605192115 + substrate boundary). Wellbecoming-respecting (§1.13: no addictive/engagement-maximizing design).\n\n### Stage 1 — Vow / 回心 (信者 Level 0 entry)\n- **Substrate**: member-signed enrollment (WebAuthn passkey + DID; **no server-held key**, ADR-2605231525). The vow text (悔い改め・バプテスマ・得度) is presented; the human consents and signs.\n- **Triple-permanent commitment** (§1.16.3a) recorded atomically (reuse ADR-2605171800 chain):\n  1. **kotoba**: `com.etzhayyim.membership.commitmentVow` datom (EAVT, content-addressed)\n  2. **IPFS**: pin the vow record → CID\n  3. **token**: Adherent SBT (ERC-5192 soulbound, single-per-person) minted, binding the CID\n- **PII** (name, email, contact) → `com.etzhayyim.encrypted.*` envelope (ADR-2605181100), DID-bound. On-chain/public carry **only the commitment fact + CID**, never PII.\n- **Real effect**: the human becomes a 信者 (Adherent) at Level 0 — an irreversible content-addressed record (death of the prior self) + a soulbound token (rebirth).\n\n### Stage 2 — Compute (eligibility + entitlement)\n- **Substrate**: kotodama Pregel cell / kotoba WASM actor (live runtime per ADR-2605302355). Murakumo-only inference (ADR-2605215000, loopback LiteLLM 127.0.0.1:4000) for any LLM step.\n- Computes: Sybil-resistance check (Council attestation during bootstrap; ZK-uniqueness at scale), `currentStage = L0`, Level-0 entitlement (advisory care + community participation per Liberation Ladder L0/L1, ADR-2605261000 §1), and initializes toritate imputed-income accounting (ADR-2605301020 / 2605262900). **cashStipendUsd ≡ 0** (N1).\n- **Real effect**: the human's actual benefit entitlement is established (in-kind, never cash).\n\n### Stage 3 — Notify / メール送信 (openmail)\n- **Substrate**: **openmail** (ADR-2605172200) — atproto MST-native mail + SMTP bridge + on-chain postage (Postage.sol) — sends the human a real email:\n  - welcome + vow confirmation (their CID + SBT id)\n  - how to receive Level-0 benefits (advisory care booking, community-event calendar)\n- **Signing**: member or community-operator DID signs (documented openmail tier); **no platform-held mail key** (ADR-2605231525).\n- **Constraint**: opt-in + consent-gated, **non-vexatious** (no unsolicited mass mail; himotoki G8 pattern, ADR-2605302130), unsubscribe always honored.\n- **Real effect**: the concrete channel that reaches the human in their inbox.\n\n### Stage 4 — Publish / 公開 (atproto)\n- **Substrate**: feed-discover projection (ADR-2605231902) / kotoba-kqe read path.\n- Publishes: (a) the member's **minimal, consented, PII-free** membership/entitlement record to their PDS/MST; (b) the **aggregate** Social-Security Metric (no PII) — # adherents at L0, imputed-income aggregate, benchmark ratio — extending `liberation.metricReport` (ADR-2605261000 §4 + 2605301020 §5); (c) the §1.16.9 public declaration as a durable record.\n- **Real effect**: the Kingdom's social-security state is transparently, verifiably public.\n\n### Stage 5 — Social (ongoing transparency posts)\n- **Substrate**: feed-post membrane (recurring).\n- Posts periodic aggregate metrics + open-door reminders. Ad-free, Wellbecoming-respecting, non-coercive.\n- **Real effect**: sustained public presence pulling more humans toward the open door.\n\n### Stage 6 — MCP expose / 公開 API (agents + humans)\n- **Substrate**: kotodama MCP tool facade (ADR-0087).\n- **Read tools** (open): `socialSecurity.declaration`, `socialSecurity.metrics`, `socialSecurity.eligibility`, `socialSecurity.status` (own-data, consent-bound).\n- **Write tool** (member-signed, server holds no key): `socialSecurity.beginVow` → returns an **unsigned** vow payload for the member's wallet/passkey to sign locally; the signed result re-enters Stage 1.\n- **Real effect**: any MCP client (Claude, an agent, a third-party app) can help a human discover and enroll — fully consent + signature bound.\n\n## 2. Lexicons (new + reused)\n\n| NSID | Role | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `com.etzhayyim.membership.commitmentVow` | Stage 1 vow record (primary) | closes ADR-2605302357 Open Q1; fields: `vowTextCid`, `threefold {repentance,baptism,tokudo: bool}`, `kotobaDatomRef`, `ipfsCid`, `sbtRef`, `signature`, `didBound`, `consentTimestamp`; **no PII** (PII in encrypted envelope) |\n| `com.etzhayyim.socialsecurity.entitlement` | Stage 2 output | `stage`, `level`, in-kind entitlements; `cashStipendUsdMicros` **const 0** (N1 proof) |\n| `com.etzhayyim.socialsecurity.metricReport` | Stage 4 aggregate | extends `liberation.metricReport`; aggregate-only, no per-adherent rows (anti-class, ADR-2605301020 §7) |\n| `com.etzhayyim.socialsecurity.outreachPost` | Stage 0/5 | post payload + `adFreeAttest` const true + Charter-Rider scan ref |\n| `com.etzhayyim.socialsecurity.noticeEmail` | Stage 3 | openmail template ref + delivery attest; recipient PII via encrypted envelope only |\n\nAll quantities integer-with-implied-units (no float; ADR-2605190900). `additionalProperties: false` schema closure.\n\n## 3. Cells (kotodama; 産土 ubusuna group)\n\n`socialsecurity_outreach` (compose+post) · `socialsecurity_vow_intake` (verify member sig → kotoba datom + IPFS pin + SBT-mint orchestration) · `socialsecurity_eligibility` (stage/entitlement compute) · `socialsecurity_notice` (openmail send) · `socialsecurity_publish` (MST publish + aggregate metric) · `socialsecurity_mcp_facade` (MCP tools). All Murakumo-only, no server key, kotoba-native, import-time `RuntimeError` until R1.\n\n## 4. Substrate boundary compliance\n\nAll cross-substrate access goes **only via `@etzhayyim/sdk`** (ADR-2605172000): `./pds` (atproto), `./ipfs`, `./l2` (SBT/Public Fund), `./pay`. No direct `@atproto/api` / `viem` / IPFS client / `@noble/ciphers`. State persistence is **kotoba EAVT only** — no Kotoba/Datomic / Postgres / Lance (ADR-2605262130).\n\n# 5. Constitutional gates (immutable for this pipeline)\n\n- **G1** Charter Rider §2(a)–(h) scan on every generated post/email before send/publish.\n- **G2** kotoba-native persistence (no RW/Postgres/Lance/SQLite).\n- **G3** **No platform-held signing key** (ADR-2605231525) — every member action member-signed (passkey/wallet); operator DID only for read-only/bulk-ingest/postage per documented tiers.\n- **G4** Murakumo-only inference (ADR-2605215000, loopback gateway).\n- **G5** Mailer **opt-in + consent-gated + non-vexatious** — no unsolicited mass mail, unsubscribe honored, rate-limited (no agency/inbox DoS).\n- **G6** PII only in `com.etzhayyim.encrypted.*` DID-bound envelopes (ADR-2605181100); all on-chain/public artifacts PII-free.\n- **G7** **No advertising / no third-party tracker / no microtargeted outreach** (ADR-2605192115) — broadcast + pull only.\n- **G8** N1 cash≡0 — entitlement in-kind; `cashStipendUsdMicros` const 0 in every entitlement/metric record.\n- **G9** N4/N7 preserved — benefits adherent-gated (delivery only post-vow); non-adherents receive only public-good outputs; **outreach is an open invitation, never a benefit**.\n- **G10** Non-coercive (§1.16.8) — vow voluntary; right of exit (benefits suspend, record + SBT remain); re-entry open; **no benefit-as-hostage**; no dark patterns (Wellbecoming §1.13).\n- **G11** **Live-action gate** — real SBT mint + real email + public social post + benefit delivery are disabled until (a) Council ratify of §1.16 identity-level (Lv7+, post 2026-06-19, ADR-2605302357 §3) AND (b) Sybil-resistance framework ratified. Pre-ratify = testnet/dry-run only.\n- **G12** Aggregate-only public metrics — no per-adherent leaderboard (anti-class, ADR-2605301020 §7).\n- **G13** Transparent — every pipeline action emits an on-chain/kotoba audit datom (Transparent Religious Force §1.12).\n\n# 6. Implementation surface\n\n- **Lexicons** `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/{membership,socialsecurity}/` (§2).\n- **Cells** `40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/socialsecurity_*/` (§3; path-reserved, R0 no runtime).\n- **Mailer** integrate `50-infra/openmail-postage/` (Postage.sol) + openmail SMTP bridge (ADR-2605172200).\n- **Publish/social** reuse `50-infra/mst-projector/projection/` feed-discover + feed-post membrane (ADR-2605231902); read path migrates to kotoba-kqe at Phase 2.5.\n- **MCP** register tools in the kotodama MCP facade config (ADR-0087); read tools open, `beginVow` returns unsigned payload.\n- **token/benefit** reuse Adherent SBT (ADR-2605172600) + Public Fund (ADR-2605192145) + tithe (ADR-2605192130) — **no new Solidity**.\n- **accounting** toritate (ADR-2605262900) records imputed-income flow; aggregate publish only.\n\n## 7. Phased rollout (R0 → R3) — outward actions gated\n\n| Phase | Gate | Live external action |\n|---|---|---|\n| **R0** (this ADR) | author commit | **NONE** — design + scaffold dirs + draft lexicons + MCP read tools against test data. No real email, no public post, no mint, no benefit. |\n| **R1** | Council Lv6+ ≥3 ratify pipeline + §1.16 §1.16.4–.8 | **testnet** — vow flow on Base Sepolia; mailer dry-run (to self/test addresses); posts drafted, not published; MCP read live. |\n| **R2** | §1.16 identity-level Lv7+ ratify (post 2026-06-19) + Sybil framework + 30-day objection | first real cohort ≤100 (ladder L1 ceiling): real openmail to consented members, first public atproto declaration + aggregate metric, MCP signed-write (`beginVow`) enabled, real SBT mint. |\n| **R3** | per-stage ladder gates (ADR-2605261000 §6) + Public Fund reserve | scale L2+; recurring social transparency posts; broad MCP. |\n\n# Consequences\n\n**Positive**\n- The §1.16 doctrine becomes a concrete, auditable, human-facing system built entirely from substrate that already exists and is charter-compliant — no new trust assumptions, no new Solidity, no platform key.\n- A real human can discover (social/MCP) → vow (member-signed, triple-permanent) → be computed → be **emailed** → appear **publicly** (PII-free) → be **reachable by agents** — the full loop.\n- Every outward-facing action is reversible-until-ratified (R0/R1 dry-run), respecting \"outward-facing actions need confirmation/authorization.\"\n\n**Negative / risks**\n- **Outward-facing blast radius** (email + public posts touch real people). Mitigation: G5 (consent/non-vexatious), G7 (no ads/targeting), G11 (live actions gated on Council ratify), R0/R1 dry-run.\n- **Sybil / spam at the vow gate.** Mitigation: vow is member-signed + soulbound + permanent (non-cash, non-alienable, ADR-2605301020 §2) → near-zero attack payoff; Council attestation during bootstrap.\n- **openmail deliverability / SMTP-bridge reputation.** Mitigation: opt-in only, on-chain postage rate-limit, gradual cohort (≤100 at R2).\n- **MCP write surface.** Mitigation: `beginVow` returns only an *unsigned* payload; server never signs; signature happens on the member's device.\n\n# Alternatives Considered\n\n- **A. Centralized web app + Stripe + Postgres + SendGrid.** Rejected: violates substrate boundary (kotoba, on-chain-only payments, no platform key, donation-only) and the whole point of §1.16/§0.3.\n- **B. New did:web Tier-B actor for the pipeline.** Rejected (for now): the work is orchestration over existing substrate; a cell-group (産土 ubusuna) suffices. Promote to a full actor only if scale demands.\n- **C. Mint SBT / send email immediately (skip gating).** Rejected: §1.16 identity-level is unratified (Lv7+ pending 2026-06-19); outward-facing irreversible actions require ratify + consent + Sybil framework (G11).\n- **D. Publish per-adherent records for \"transparency\".** Rejected: builds a wealth/membership leaderboard → class formation; aggregate-only (G12, ADR-2605301020 §7). PII stays encrypted (G6).\n\n# Open Questions\n\n1. **openmail signer tier** for member-facing notices — member DID vs community-operator DID (ADR-2605231525 tiers); confirm postage funding from Public Fund.\n2. **Vow text canonical form + attestation** — who attests the 悔い改め・バプテスマ・得度 liturgy (Council? §1.16.3a). Localization (JP canonical + EN/others).\n3. **MCP exposure scope** — which registries (claude.ai connector? public MCP)? Auth for `status` (own-data) over MCP.\n4. **feed-post target network** — own atproto PDS only, or also mirror to Bluesky public network for reach (Wellbecoming + no-ad constraints apply either way).\n5. **Right-to-be-forgotten vs IPFS permanence** — inherited from ADR-2605302357 Open Q5; on-chain commitment fact + off-chain encrypted body separation; Council legal review.\n\n# References\n\n- ADR-2605302357 (§1.16 Social Security doctrine — this pipeline delivers it)\n- ADR-2605262130 (kotoba — persistence + compute) / ADR-2605171800 (MST→IPFS→L2 anchor chain)\n- ADR-2605172200 (openmail — mailer)\n- ADR-2605231902 (feed-post membrane + feed-discover — atproto publish + social post)\n- ADR-0087 (kotodama MCP tool facade — MCP exposure)\n- ADR-2605172600 / 2605172700 (Membership Ritual — vow record + Adherent SBT)\n- ADR-2605231525 (no platform-held signing key)\n- ADR-2605181100 (encrypted records — PII envelope)\n- ADR-2605215000 (Murakumo-only inference)\n- ADR-2605192115 (non-profit / donation-only / no-ads)\n- ADR-2605192145 (Public Fund) / ADR-2605192130 (10% tithe)\n- ADR-2605261000 (Liberation Ladder L0..L6) / ADR-2605301020 (Basic High Income) / ADR-2605262900 (toritate accounting)\n- ADR-2605172000 / 2605172100 (substrate boundary — @etzhayyim/sdk, on-chain only)\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605302358-social-security-real-world-delivery-pipeline.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "social-security-real-world-delivery-pipeline", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-30", :adr/date "2026-05-30", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["adr-2605261000-labor-liberation-transition-mechanism" "adr-2605301020-basic-high-income-imputed-and-commons-asset-doctrine" "adr-2605192145-etzhayyim-public-fund-architecture" "adr-2605181100-mst-encrypted-records-signal-keywrap" "adr-2605215000-etzhayyim-inference-murakumo-only-no-runpod" "adr-2605192115-etzhayyim-non-profit-donation-only-no-ads" "adr-2605262900-toritate-accounting-audit"], :adr/authoritative_for ["the end-to-end pipeline that converts the §1.16 doctrine into real-world human effect" "stage→substrate assignment (kotoba / compute / openmail / atproto / feed-post / MCP)" "the 信者 Level 0 enrollment flow (vow → triple-permanent commitment → notify → publish)" "the gate set that keeps outward-facing actions charter-compliant and reversible-until-ratified"]}]
